      "summaries": {
        "en": "systemd is a Linux system and service manager that replaces traditional init systems by providing faster boot times and unified service management. Its technical innovation lies in using socket activation and dependency-based parallel startup, which reduces resource waste and improves system responsiveness. Developers can use systemd to create custom service units, manage daemons efficiently, and implement system-level automation through its comprehensive logging and monitoring tools.",
        "zh": "systemd 是一个现代化的 Linux 系统和服务管理器，它取代了传统的 init 系统，通过并行启动服务和基于依赖关系的管理，显著提升了系统启动速度和服务响应能力。其核心设计采用套接字激活机制，仅在服务真正需要时才分配资源，这种按需启动的理念减少了系统开销。在实际应用中，开发者可以编写 systemd 单元文件来定义自定义服务，利用其强大的日志管理工具 journald 进行故障排查，并通过 systemctl 命令轻松控制守护进程，实现高效的系统运维和自动化部署。",
        "es": "systemd is a Linux system and service manager that replaces traditional init systems by providing faster boot times and unified service management. Its technical innovation lies in using socket activation and dependency-based parallel startup, which reduces resource waste and improves system responsiveness. Developers can use systemd to create custom service units, manage daemons efficiently, and implement system-level automation through its comprehensive logging and monitoring tools.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "systemd stands out for c, init, and linux in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "systemd is a Linux system and service manager that replaces traditional init systems by providing faster boot times and unified service management. Its technical innovation lies in using socket activation and dependency-based parallel startup, which reduces resource waste and improves system responsiveness. Developers can use systemd to create custom service units, manage daemons efficiently, and implement system-level automation through its comprehensive logging and monitoring tools.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/systemd/systemd for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
